# Compiles every CrossByte class that is available on Node.
#
# Node is a JavaScript target with an operating system behind it, so it sits
# between the browser and a native build: hxnodejs supplies a filesystem and a
# process environment, but there is no sys.thread, no sys.db, and sys.net.Socket
# is a partial stand-in without select(). What that leaves is checked here.
#
# Paired with ci/js-build.hxml. The two differ only in -lib hxnodejs, which is
# what defines `nodejs` and so decides every `js && !nodejs` gate in the tree.
-cp src
-lib hxnodejs
--macro include('crossbyte')
--js export/node/crossbyte.js
